WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:06.240
Here is a teeny-tiny closed
cast-on that is perfect for lace.

2
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:11.840
It's basically a small hung hem.
Start by casting on every other needle

3
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.520
with scrap yarn.
Because I'm going to be knitting in lace.

4
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.400
I used my ribber cast-on
comb for even weight.

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.200
This isn't required,
but it really works great.

6
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.000
Then knit one row of ravel cord.

7
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.360
With your main yarn at your garment

8
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:34.840
a tension knit three rows
over every other needle.

9
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:44.120
Pick up the open Cast-on stitches
and hang them on the empty needles.

10
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.960
KNit 2 or 3 rows plain
and start the lace pattern.

11
00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:10.440
The edge is permanent,
stretchy and almost invisible.

